<div>
  <div>
    <div class="p-3">
      <div class="funcard2 px-3 py-4" style="color:rgb(255, 246, 167);">
        <div class="text-center mb-4">
          <h3>Welcome to goVend</h3>
          <h1 class="h3">Increase sales and stay organized</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center">
          <%= image_tag "favicon.png", alt:"vendor booth", class:"img-fluid cat mb-4", style: "max-width: 150px; height: auto;" %>
        </div>
        <p class="lead" style="font-size: 1.1rem;">It is a big task to find events to sell your products at, stay organized, keep track of the events, check payment status, worrying if you applied to them, and most embarassingly of all, double booking. Let's fix that.</p>
        <p class="lead" style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Made with love by a vendor, for vendors and events. Click the menu to get started.</p>
      </div>
  <div class="row funcard2 px-3 py-4 mt-4" style="color:rgb(255, 246, 167);">
    <div class="col-12 p-2">
      <h2 class="text-center mb-4">About</h2>
      <div class="mb-4">
        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;"><strong>VENDORS:</strong> Allow me to simplify your life. goVend is a platform that connects vendors to events. It allows you to search for events, apply to them, and keep track of the events you have attended. It also allows you to create events and search for vendors. </p>
        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;"><strong>EVENT COORDINATORS:</strong> Allow me to simplify your life as well. Here, you share your events and find vendors. Find new exciting vendors and the latest trends through ambitious businesses to keep your patrons happy.  </p>
        <p class="text-center font-weight-bold mt-3">Setup in less than 5 minutes!</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="h4 text-center mb-3">Fast Account Setup</h3>
        <ol class="pl-4">
          <li class="mb-2"> Sign up and start finding events in less than 5 minutes.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"> Create a profile to showcase your business.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="h4 text-center mb-3">So many perks</h3>
        <ul class="pl-4">
          <li class="mb-2"> Easily host events you want to share with a simple setup.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"> Once you have created an event, it becomes searchable to all users.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"> Search for events that are looking for vendors!</li>
          <li class="mb-2"> View a hosts page to see their other hosted events.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"> Create a list of your events and update the status.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"> Track your event data.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>


    <div class="cube-gallery-wrapper py-5">
      <input class="radio-button" type="radio" name="cube-gallery" checked/>
      <input class="radio-button" type="radio" name="cube-gallery"/>
      <input class="radio-button" type="radio" name="cube-gallery"/>
      <input class="radio-button" type="radio" name="cube-gallery"/>
      <input class="radio-button" type="radio" name="cube-gallery"/>
      <input class="radio-button" type="radio" name="cube-gallery"/>
      <div class="cube-container mt-4">
        <div class="cube">
          <% upcoming_events = Event.where('started_at > ?', Date.today).order(:started_at).limit(6) %>
          <% upcoming_events.each do |event| %>
            <div class="cube-side d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center">
              <div class="text-center p-3">
                <div class="mb-2">
                  <% if event.photo.present? %>
                    <%= image_tag url_for(event.photo.url), class: "img-fluid rounded", style: "max-height: 100px; width: auto;", alt: "event photo" %>
                  <% else %>
                    <%= image_tag "bulb.png", class: "img-fluid", style: "max-height: 100px; width: auto;", alt: "default photo" %>
                  <% end %>
                </div>
                <h2 class="h5 mb-1 px-2"><%= event.name %></h2>
                <h4 class="cube-text h6 mb-2"><%= event.started_at.strftime("%A, %B %d, %Y") %></h4>
                <p class="small mb-0">Create an account view all events.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
</div>
